-- X5 (SHADOW-SEMANTICS S1-PRELUDE (a), matrix row 49) -- x4's CONSTRAINED twin.
--
-- x4 collides with an UNCONSTRAINED prelude standalone (`isEven : Int -> Bool`).  This one
-- collides with a CONSTRAINED one: `count` is `stdlib/core.mdk`'s
-- `export count : Foldable t => (a -> <e> Bool) -> t a -> <e> Int`.  The distinction is
-- load-bearing rather than decorative, because elaboration PREPENDS a `$dict` parameter to
-- a `=>`-constrained prelude function -- so the two cells stress the same rule against
-- callee shapes that differ by one argument, and an implementation that gets the name's
-- denotation wrong fails them in two different ways (a silently wrong exit-0 value at x4's
-- shape, an under-applied callee at this one).  Pinning only the unconstrained cell would
-- leave the arity-shifted path ungraded.
--
--   RULED (S1-PRELUDE (a)): the implicit prelude is in neither half of S1's left-operand
--     kind partition, so the prelude `count` creates no shadow.  The bare `count` is the
--     INTERFACE METHOD, `impl Sized Box` is at the receiver's head, and the impl body
--     returns the payload => `7`.  <== what this fixture pins.
--   REJECTED reading (the prelude standalone takes the name): the call routes to a
--     two-parameter, dict-carrying callee with one argument.
--
-- EXPECTED VALUE HAND-DERIVED FROM THE RULING, NOT CAPTURED (see x4's header for why this
-- corpus does not capture here).  At the time this was written the arms disagreed: #1492 --
-- `check` clean, built binary `7`, `medaka run` E-PANIC `intToString: not an Int`.
--
-- RECEIVER PROVENANCE: `Box 7` is a GROUNDED constructor application, the complement of
-- x4's ungrounded numeric literal.  Same rule, both provenances.
interface Sized c where
  count : c -> Int

data Box = Box Int

impl Sized Box where
  count (Box n) = n

main = println (count (Box 7))
